From: Claude <claude@local>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 08:38:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the admin dashboard mobile responsive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The dashboard shell had a fixed 224px sidebar always visible, which
would eat most of a phone screen — this was desktop-only by
construction, not just untested on mobile.

- components/dashboard-shell.tsx (new): sidebar becomes a slide-in
  drawer below the lg breakpoint (fixed position, backdrop overlay,
  closes on backdrop tap or on navigating), and stays static/always-
  visible above it — standard responsive-drawer pattern
- Header: hamburger toggle appears only below lg; email hides below
  sm (just sign-out button remains) to leave room on narrow screens
- sidebar.tsx: added an optional onNavigate callback so tapping a nav
  link closes the mobile drawer automatically
- (dashboard)/layout.tsx: now just fetches the user and delegates to
  DashboardShell, all the drawer logic lives in one client component
- All 6 data tables (Errands, Transactions, Accounts list, Account
  detail x1, Payouts x2) now wrap in an overflow-x-auto container
  nested inside the existing rounded card, so wide tables scroll
  horizontally on narrow screens instead of breaking the layout

Verified with a real `next build` — all 8 routes still compile clean.
